UID:10035722-1775239200-1777827600@www.riverartsdistrict.com
SUMMARY:Anastasiia Avramchuk: The Garden of Quiet Resistance exhibition
DESCRIPTION:In a world shaped by war\, displacement\, and a growing sense of uncertainty\, the act of creating and observing beauty becomes a quiet form of resistance. This exhibition of botanical drawings explores inner calm not as an escape from reality\, but as a way of remaining present\, attentive\, and grounded. Through plants\, light\, and careful observation\, the works reflect a belief that even in fragile conditions\, life continues to grow and quietly persist. \nAnastasiia Avramchuk is a Ukrainian botanical artist and designer from Kyiv\, currently based in North Carolina. She works with ink\, watercolor\, colored pencils\, and digital illustration\, focusing on the quiet resilience and structural beauty of plant life. She is a member of the Society of Ukrainian Botanical Artists. Her work has received international recognition\, including the Best Debut award at the Botanical Art Ukraine exhibition in 2021. In 2024\, her watercolor Casuarina equisetifolia was selected among the top three works at the international exhibition Rare Plants of the World in Kyiv. \n\nhttps://avramchuk.art/ \nhttps://www.instagram.com/anastasyavram
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/anastasiia-avramchuk-the-garden-of-quiet-resistance-exhibition/
LOCATION:Pink Dog Gallery\, 348 Depot Street\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/AnastasiiaAvramchukB_sq.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Pink Dog Creative":MAILTO:hedy@pinkdog-creative.com
GEO:35.5819169;-82.5643273
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Pink Dog Gallery 348 Depot Street Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=348 Depot Street:geo:-82.5643273,35.5819169
END:VEVENT
