SUMMARY:How Long Will It Last? A contemplation on impermanence\, grief and flowers
DESCRIPTION:“How long will it last?” is a common question in a florist’s career and a mirror to our impermanence. Inspired by the reverence\, companionship\, and guidance of a death doula\, we want to invite the public to hold hands with existence and mortality. \nFascinated by the ephemeral\, the objective is to create an immersive portrayal of the transitions from life to death in a way that challenges our measure of worth by longevity and durability. Our installation will be composed of flowers and plant material and enhanced by play of light\, reflection\, height\, and poignant ephemera to envelope participants in the spectrum of transience and grief. \nThe creative team is: Hanna Zahory\, Grace Bates-Toulson\, Allison Omlor and Gabrielle Thompson
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/how-long-will-it-last-a-contemplation-on-impermanence-grief-and-flowers/
LOCATION:Trackside Studios\, 375 Depot Street\, Asheville\, 28801
CATEGORIES:Events,Second Saturday Art Strolls
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/how-long-will-it-last-_-square.jpg
GEO:35.5805429;-82.5646109
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Trackside Studios 375 Depot Street Asheville 28801;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=375 Depot Street:geo:-82.5646109,35.5805429
END:VEVENT
